2026-10-19T19:51:50.6915141Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
2026-10-19T19:51:50.6924069Z [1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer[0m
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7012120Z [32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7020237Z [0m
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7020615Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7021074Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7021309Z 
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7021882Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7022555Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7022861Z 
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7023080Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7023574Z    if you are ready to continue.
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7023807Z 
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7024372Z 3. Create the system users [34m(uids [30001..30008])[0m and groups [34m(gid 30000)[0m
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7024936Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7025266Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7025545Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7025677Z 
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7026088Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7026371Z 
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7026598Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7027149Z    can use Nix.
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7027323Z 
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7027459Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7027657Z 
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7028073Z [32m[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7028583Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7033626Z 
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7034007Z I will:
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7034407Z 
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7034679Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7035183Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7035652Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7035982Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7036203Z  - install Nix in /nix
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7036447Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7036797Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7037333Z    /root
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7049497Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7050019Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7060600Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7061139Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7061354Z 
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7062694Z [32m[4;32mReady to continue?
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7063266Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7081390Z 
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7081899Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7091877Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7092427Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7092730Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7092876Z 
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7093006Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7093170Z 
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7093307Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7093586Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7093734Z 
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7093813Z If you would like to
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7094004Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7094125Z 
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7094258Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-19T19:51:50.7094507Z   $ sh ./install-nix
